    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "antigravity",
          "informationUri": "internal:agy",
          "rules": [{ "id": "antigravity.graph-chunk-overwrite" }]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "antigravity.graph-chunk-overwrite",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "agy (gemini-3.1-pro-high, cross-vendor advisory arm), reviewing head 23f058b6ba in a disposable tree, reported: 'When PREFILL_GRAPH=1 is enabled, prefill_all_layers_gpu ignores the passed positions and unconditionally replays a captured graph configured for 0..S-1 and an empty KV cache. Subsequent chunks in the generate_2.rs loop will reset kv_cache_lengths to 0 and overwrite the first chunk's KV data at offset 0, permanently corrupting the prefill state for prompts longer than rows.' (grounding: asserted, agy's own). Independently reverified by the primary reviewer reading prefill_graphed_replay directly: agreed. FIXED at this subject (31cd3f6c40, commit 66c07c49dc): prefill.rs now gates the graph path with graph_may_run(enabled, positions) = enabled && positions.first()==Some(&0), so only a chunk starting at position 0 may replay a graph; every later chunk now runs eager. Re-verified by the primary reviewer: read the diff (prefill.rs only, +29/-1) and ran `cargo test -p aprender-serve --lib --features cuda -- graph_chunk_tests_3715 dense_prefill_chunk_tests` on intel -- 4 passed, 0 failed, rc=0."
          },
